<title>UK: Hodder Headline appoints Weston chairman.</title>
<headline>Hodder Headline appoints Weston chairman.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>British publisher Hodder Headline said on Thursday that it had appointed Christopher Weston as its chairman to succeed the Earl of Donoughmore who retires at the group's next annual meeting in May 1997.</p>
<p>Weston, 59, has been a director of the group since it was founded in 1986. He is also the chairman and chief executive of auctioneers Philips, Son and Neale and also Glendining &amp; Co.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
